WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions for the approved 77-second ARIA R4 commercial. Timings come from the narration timing
map (danceflow-aria-video/TIMING_MAP_R1.md) and the cut edit decisions; R4 keeps the same
narration clock.

1
00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:03.200
Most business software keeps records.

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.900
Most AI waits for you to ask a question.

3
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:08.800
I don't.

4
00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:13.400
I'm ARIA, the AI team member inside DanceFlow,

5
00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:19.300
working while you're focused on your business,
keeping track of what needs attention across the operation.

6
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:25.600
A package running low, an unanswered inquiry,
a client who's gone quiet, a class that's nearly full.

7
00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.450
I don't handle everything the same way.

8
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:30.500
You decide how I work.

9
00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:32.900
Some things I can handle automatically.

10
00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:35.000
Some wait for your approval.

11
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:38.100
Others I simply bring to your attention.

12
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:42.300
And when it comes to money,
those decisions stay with you.

13
00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:46.160
Because DanceFlow isn't just software that keeps records.

14
00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:50.000
It's an operating platform built to help do the work,

15
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:55.330
from the moment a dancer finds a studio,
reaches out, and keeps coming back,

16
00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:59.500
DanceFlow connects the people
and the work behind your business.

17
00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:05.650
Studios, instructors, organizers, dancers:
one connected place.

18
00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:09.000
I'm ARIA, and I'm here to help you run it.

19
00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:17.000
DanceFlow.
Software that helps do the work—not just track it.
